<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Matthias, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1557">1557</a>–<a href="/years/1619">1619</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Matthias was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> from 1612 to 1619 and King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, a son of Emperor Maximilian II. As archduke he challenged his brother Rudolf II and in 1608, backed by the estates of Hungary, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, forced Rudolf to cede him those lands. His reign ended amid the Bohemian revolt that began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/matthias-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Matthias, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas van Valckenborch · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucas_van_Valckenborch_-_Emperor_Matthias_as_Archduke,_with_baton.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1608, led by Karel the Elder of Žerotín, they sided with <b>Archduke Matthias</b> against Emperor Rudolf II and had their liberties confirmed.</blockquote><a href="/empire/margraviate-of-moravia">Margraviate of Moravia · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=48.21,16.37&amp;year=1597" aria-label="Vienna on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4931 477 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Matthias, Holy Roman Emperor"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5381 747h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5381 747h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=48.21,16.37&amp;year=1597">What was here in 1597? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
